comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-13T18:12:30.417Z","harness:codex","{\"text\":\"Duplicate check: complete live all-status corpus2953 items with zero omissions/unreadable records plus request search/open/in-progress reads. Full live pm-xm7c and pm-y9hq are closed for shipped CLI/MCP and SDK atomic mutations; pm-xm7c history67 entries verifies current hash. No existing open JSONL/keyed-upsert owner was found. Current pm item mutate contract exposes required --transaction-id, --stdin-json and --dry-run; GH report incorrectly states no CLI bulk primitive. Remaining discoverability/JSONL/upsert request is additive.\"}"
  "2026-10-13T18:39:47.760Z","harness:codex","Hosted static CI38446450129 correctly caught the missing expected_result in this newly created intake. Added the explicit intended outcome through PM without changing acceptance criteria, implementation scope or gate thresholds. This planning correction does not claim the reported feature/defect is implemented."
  "2026-10-15T12:29:33.446Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation note (2026-10-15): bulk creation lands on the existing atomic surface instead of a new top-level command. The SDK resolver now accepts JSON Lines, single records, and op-less create documents (pm create field names, optionally wrapped as {ref, item}); records without ref/id receive row-<n> aliases; declared schema fields are admitted on create/update option rows via their option targets. A new planner, planItemMutationDocument, reads the workspace (schema hydration also under the configuration-only dry-run scope, where declared fields otherwise vanish), derives a stable transaction id from the document bytes when none is given, and resolves --upsert-key against existing items (custom or core field): one match becomes an update (rows[].upserted), a missing key, an in-batch duplicate, or several matches refuse before any write. CLI adds --from <path> and --upsert-key and makes --transaction-id optional; MCP pm_mutate accepts item rows, upsertKey and an optional transactionId. pm create many refuses with bulk_create_route and names the route. The journal/plan mismatch is now a typed transaction_plan_mismatch refusal instead of an unknown_error.\n\nMeasured in a sandbox: 2-record JSON Lines import committed in one transaction; replay returned recovered:true with no duplicates; upsert by external_id updated the matched item and created the unmatched one; dry-run under the configuration-only scope validated with the declared field present.\n"
  "2026-10-15T15:46:12.065Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit full review, 2026-10-15): (1) keyed upsert no longer matches the ids this document itself would create (deterministic ids from the transaction id, plus explicit create ids), so a committed import re-run with --upsert-key and a derived transaction id keeps its original create plan and the journal recovers it (recovered:true) instead of refusing with transaction_plan_mismatch; integration test added. (2) options-based create rows that become updates keep their declared runtime-field option keys (externalId) instead of dropping them. Both covered by unit tests. Hosted CI also required escape_class and structured gate_evidence on the closed Issues of this change (defect-evidence gate), now recorded.\n"
  "2026-10-15T18:12:26.102Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit): the docs/SDK.md planItemMutationDocument upsert example gave the second row no external_id, so the documented upsert_key_missing refusal would have stopped it; the row now carries ext-2 so the example runs as written."
  "2026-10-15T19:01:37.296Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, third pass): keyed upsert converted a matched create row to an update and deleted its ref before reference collection, so a later row addressing it as @ref failed with Unknown mutation reference and the rows receipt omitted that ref. The matched alias is now recorded against the existing id before conversion, and the receipt reads aliases from the input rows, so upserted rows keep their ref and later rows resolve @ref to the matched item."
  "2026-10-15T19:59:27.660Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, fourth pass): the suggested unconditional exact-title refusal in planItemMutationDocument was not adopted. Every create row already runs the full SDK create path in both the staged dry-run and the commit, so governance.duplicate_detection_mode (strict refuses, advisory warns, off opts out, --allow-duplicate honoured) applies per row exactly as for pm create. The dry-run receipt does, however, discard the per-row advisory warnings; that gap is owned by pm-ekf2gu."
  "2026-10-15T20:59:29.642Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, fifth pass): stableUpsertValue serialized non-string key values with JSON.stringify, so two equivalent object values with different key insertion order never matched and the row stayed a create. Plain-object keys are now sorted recursively before serialization (arrays keep their order), and the unit spec covers an object-valued upsert key matching on content."
  "2026-10-15T22:05:50.670Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, sixth pass): keyed upsert was resolved before the writer lock and never re-checked, so two concurrent plans with different transaction ids could each create an item for the same key value. Create rows that matched nothing now carry a unique {key,value} guard; commitItemMutations and previewItemMutations re-check it under the lock through a per-transaction lazily scanned index (own create ids excluded so replays stay recovered) and refuse with upsert_key_conflict before any write. A re-run re-plans the row as an update. Schema and candidate helpers moved from the planner into item-transaction (resolveTransactionSchema, listUpsertKeyCandidates); MCP pm_mutate rows admit unique; docs/COMMANDS.md and docs/SDK.md describe the guard; unit and integration tests cover the race, the preview, the replay, and malformed guards."
  "2026-10-15T23:54:45.176Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, eighth pass): canonicalizeUpsertValue sorted object keys with localeCompare, which can report distinct keys (precomposed and decomposed e-acute) as equal, so insertion order could leak into the canonical JSON and the planner or the lock-held guard could miss an existing key. Keys now sort by code units; the unit spec covers collating-equal keys in different orders."
  "2026-10-16T01:01:52.835Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, ninth pass): a keyed-upsert row that matched before the writer lock became a plain update by id, so a concurrent writer could change or remove the key after planning and the update would still land. Converted rows now carry match {key,value}; the update step re-reads the key under the lock and refuses with upsert_match_changed (CONFLICT) before writing. Verifying the re-run path exposed a second gap: a compensated attempt under a derived transaction id refused the re-planned document with transaction_plan_mismatch because the journal still demanded the old step ids. parseJournal now treats a compensated journal as holding nothing to resume, so the re-plan starts attempt 2 under the same id while applying, compensating, and committed journals still replay only their own plan. Unit tests cover the journal rule and the guard shapes; the integration race test covers the moved key, the preview, and the re-plan commit."
  "2026-10-16T01:57:42.307Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, tenth pass): three more planner gaps closed. An explicit ref equal to the row-<n> alias a later row would be synthesized surfaced only as a misleading 'Duplicate mutation ref'; synthesis now refuses up front naming the colliding row and the reserved prefix. An options row carrying a declared field whose metadata_key differs from its option name (key classification, metadata_key escape_class) was reported as upsert_key_missing because readUpsertKeyValue only tried the metadata key and its camelCase form; it now resolves the declared option target first. The MCP pm_mutate commit phase built its extension scope from the raw path while plan and preview used the resolved root; all three phases now share one scope."
  "2026-10-16T03:58:40.504Z","harness:codex","PR #1479 final closeout: live strict full corpus contains 2,971 readable items with no omissions and zero initially in progress. DeepScan on 578c5277 identifies a possible null dereference in the MCP bulk-import integration test; added an explicit response-content guard before reading result, preserving all assertions. Existing unresolved review 4289801784 is implemented by e215ab324: converted upsert updates carry match guards checked inside the workspace writer lock, with the real moved-key/re-plan integration regression. Windows Node24 packed check was cancelled, not passed; the next head must complete it. GitHub currently reports zero open Dependabot, secret-scanning, or code-scanning alerts. Other items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-10-16T04:02:37.897Z","harness:codex","Further inspection of unresolved CodeRabbit thread 4289801784 found the prior fix re-read the key under the workspace transaction lock but before the per-item lock. Ordinary pm update does not acquire the workspace transaction lock. Move the existing match check into the item store precondition scope, after the target item lock and read, while retaining the public update pipeline. Add a deterministic race regression that uses a separate ordinary CLI writer at the item-lock acquisition boundary and verifies its key change and history survive the refusal. The earlier comment describes only workspace-lock coverage, not protection against ordinary writers."
  "2026-10-16T04:09:48.749Z","harness:codex","Manual bulk-intake acceptance: the existing public item mutate surface committed pm-gh1478, pm-gh1481, and pm-gh1482 as one three-row transaction, with an input-ordered receipt. An initial options-shaped request incorrectly supplied numeric estimatedMinutes instead of its declared string type and returned an untyped e.trim error; correcting the scalar representation and replaying the compensated transaction committed all three once (recovered:true). This exposes an additional raw-options refusal-quality case for the existing recovery-closure lineage. Canonical pm-srns reused for GH1480; pm-7zs0 reused for the current release blocker1483. None of these intake-only owners are claimed."
  "2026-10-16T04:23:50.926Z","harness:codex","The deterministic ordinary-writer regression fails on prior head578c5277 because the import incorrectly commits. Extended the same test to unprefixed SDK item ids: the initial scope missed the canonical locked id and the new case failed the same way. The guard now resolves canonical identity before entering the unchanged public update pipeline, then validates the actual document after the item lock is acquired. Full and unprefixed ids preserve the competing update and history on refusal. The first broad local run passed10515 tests but failed one packed-continuation prerequisite because npm/package.json was not exposed to module resolution; the same packed Node/Bun continuation test passes with the installed npm package exposed through NODE_PATH. No assertion or coverage gate was changed."
  "2026-10-16T04:25:15.757Z","harness:codex","Final linked verification passes both recorded commands:77 bulk/planner/preview/CLI/MCP cases plus the nested/concurrent precondition-scope test. The ordinary-writer matrix covers full and unprefixed ids. The packed continuation prerequisite is repaired by exposing the already installed npm module through NODE_PATH; its full Node and Bun public-SDK oracle passes. Final typecheck and static quality now run serially so another local build cannot change dist beneath their subprocess probes."
  "2026-10-16T04:26:07.594Z","harness:codex","Tracker integrity evidence: current health check returns ok with history_drift ok, and full validation finds zero hash/chain/version/workspace-state mismatches. Existing legacy resolution warnings remain170 terminal items and are not represented as newly fixed. Live GitHub reports1478/1481/1482 have new open unclaimed child records;1480 reuses pm-srns,1483 reuses pm-7zs0, and the raw-options scalar failure has open child pm-bulk-option-validation under pm-f05lsg. Terminal pm-jsm9im resolution now accurately describes full-depth metadata/key/body checks in both item formats and explicitly distinguishes open output-compaction fault1478."
  "2026-10-16T04:38:02.233Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: all four TypeScript projects and both linked commands pass (78 cases). Negative controls prove the ordinary-writer race on the previous head and the shortened-ID bypass before their fixes. The serial static run passed source, dependency, export, documentation, lint, contract, SDK, token, graph, and package gates before record-integrity found this reopened item missing expected_result. Reopening cleared terminal evidence; the atomic close below restores a current expected/actual contract. Rerun record-integrity and the remaining bounded mutation gate after closure. The earlier broad coverage run failed only because npm/package.json was absent from module resolution; the repaired packed Node/Bun oracle passes and final full coverage will run with NODE_PATH configured."
  "2026-10-16T04:45:26.525Z","harness:codex","Post-closure verification passes: generated changelog check through latest pm-changelog 2026.10.15 (2677 entries), terminal defect evidence (zero findings), full record-integrity assurance, bounded mutation gate (341 killed and seven classified equivalents across 348 mutations), npx/bunx smoke across nine packages, and the unchanged package artifact budget. All prior static components passed on the same frozen source; record-integrity now passes with the restored closure evidence. Canonical full coverage and hosted current-head checks will run after this reviewed closeout commit. Only the actively implemented owner was claimed, and no in-progress claims remain."
  "2026-10-16T05:21:49.902Z","harness:codex","Verification correction: the prior local static run stopped at tracker-context-quality when reopened expected_result was missing, so the earlier summary overstated completion of later static components. The exact hosted head reached graph-composition and found 12 newly introduced prose-only pairs. Eleven represent real delivery/ownership relationships and are now typed related edges. The remaining reference explicitly rejects a historical shell-completion issue as a duplicate and is recorded in the existing targeted false-positive ledger; all numeric bounds remain unchanged. Full static quality will run after closure. The pre-review source passed 10517 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Nine new regression cases failed before the four valid product fixes; the focused three-file suite now passes 60 tests."
  "2026-10-16T05:32:02.419Z","harness:codex","Final review remediation passes all three linked commands: 106 tests, including direct SDK duplicate-guard validation in preview and commit, JSON versus JSONL diagnostics, wrapped document ID precedence, and canonical identity under the actual item lock. Nine regressions failed on the pre-fix source; the corrected focused suite passes. The connected text-format owner adds eight passing cases (114 combined). Historical package measurements now have an audited qualification and a controlled archive comparison; the original immutable history is preserved and its verification passes. The earlier parent head passed 10517 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; current full static and hosted coverage still require the final frozen-head run."
  "2026-10-16T05:36:21.576Z","harness:codex","Final static reached the generated error-code catalog check and correctly detected that direct SDK duplicate-upsert refusal adds another emitting source. Regenerated the catalog with pnpm contracts:errors:update; the public code and recovery contract are unchanged. Four-project typecheck and the terminal defect-evidence gate pass. Rerunning the complete static command after this generated-source refresh."
  "2026-10-16T05:40:18.547Z","harness:codex","Regenerated the runtime contract fixture after refreshing its SDK error catalog dependency. The generated diff only adds sdk/item-transaction.ts to the existing upsert_key_duplicate emitting sources. No error code, schema, threshold or refusal policy changes. Full static will be rerun with both generated artifacts synchronized."
  "2026-10-16T06:02:18.466Z","harness:codex","Final frozen-source package checks pass: npx and bunx smoke across nine packages; artifact gate retains the unchanged20000000 first-party-byte ceiling with19100342 bytes/1678 files and the complete4745-file runtime closure. Graph composition and record integrity pass; all114 linked functional cases pass. Four TypeScript projects, generated contracts, terminal defect evidence, version consistency and tracked-secret scan pass. Latest pm-changelog2026.10.15 generates/checks the changelog. The complete local static command did not pass: qualified SDK/CLI performance failures and a bounded-mutation timeout are retained in the related canonical diagnosis, with no relaxed budget or timeout reclassification. Complete final-head hosted static/coverage acceptance remains mandatory before merge. Required telemetry reliability passes at2.84 percent failures with zero missing error-code rows; Sentry correctly blocks release on the two separately tracked faults. Fresh trace/span discovery is empty, so ingestion is not claimed. All27 open GitHub issues have PM-link comments, all three security-alert inventories are empty, and the only open PR is this delivery."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T04:25:15.096Z","harness:codex",A workspace transaction lock serializes bulk transactions but does not fence ordinary item writers. Revalidate a planned match against the same document read under the target item lock; resolve shortened SDK ids to canonical identity before scoping a target-specific guard. Prove the race at the actual item-lock boundary with a separate ordinary writer and verify its history remains intact.
